is vendored verbatim from that project's v3/helpers.py (the LayoutLMv3
input-encoding and logit-to-order decoding routines: DataCollator,
boxes2inputs, prepare_inputs, parse_logits, check_duplicate). It carries a
CC BY-NC-SA attribution header and is unmodified.

The "layoutreader" reading-order backend at
    src/rare/models/order/layoutreader.py
is original RaRe code (Apache-2.0), but it calls the helpers above and loads
the `hantian/layoutreader` LayoutLMv3 checkpoint
(https://huggingface.co/hantian/layoutreader), which is likewise released
under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Using this backend therefore carries the NonCommercial
restriction, whether or not the helpers file is redistributed.

That project is itself a LayoutLMv3-based reimplementation of LayoutReader,
originally published by Microsoft Research
(https://github.com/microsoft/unilm/tree/master/layoutreader); see the
Citation section of README.md.